     {
      "id": "7154a9b",
      "elType": "widget",
      "widgetType": "heading",
      "isInner": false,
      "settings": {
       "title": "What Is a Tech Pack and Why Do You Need One?",
       "header_size": "h2",
       "mf_motion": "reveal"
      },
      "elements": []
     },
     {
      "id": "e97ec79",
      "elType": "widget",
      "widgetType": "text-editor",
      "isInner": false,
      "settings": {
       "editor": "<p>A tech pack (technical package) is a detailed document that tells your manufacturer exactly how to build your garment. It covers measurements, materials, stitching, trims, labels, and construction details — so your sample comes out right the first time.</p><p>Without a tech pack, you risk:</p><ul><li>Wrong measurements and sizing</li><li>Incorrect fabrics or trims</li><li>Multiple costly sample rounds</li><li>Miscommunication with the factory</li></ul>",
       "__globals__": {
        "typography_typography": "globals/typography?id=text"
       },
       "_animation": "fadeIn",
       "_animation_delay": 0
      },
      "elements": []
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
